<h2 id="standard">1. Standard applied</h2>
<p>
  This site aims to conform to the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA</strong>, the
  standard referenced by the European Accessibility Act and by the Swedish
  <span lang="sv">lag (2018:1937) om tillgänglighet till digital offentlig service</span>.
</p>
<p>
  As a personal, non-commercial site run by a private individual, it is not legally required to meet that standard.
  It is applied because a portfolio that some people cannot read is a portfolio that has failed.
</p>

<h2 id="done">2. What has been done</h2>
<ul>
  <li>All text and interface colours checked against WCAG contrast ratios in both light and dark themes, at 4.5:1 or
    better for body text.</li>
  <li>Every icon-only control carries a text label for screen readers; decorative icons are hidden from them.</li>
  <li>The whole site is operable by keyboard: menus open and close with <kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Escape</kbd>, focus is
    visible on every interactive element, and off-screen menus are kept out of the tab order.</li>
  <li>A "skip to main content" link is the first focusable element on every page.</li>
  <li>Form fields have permanently associated labels, correct autocomplete hints, and errors announced to assistive
    technology rather than shown only in colour.</li>
  <li>Images carry meaningful alternative text; purely decorative images are marked as such.</li>
  <li>Animation is suppressed for anyone whose system requests reduced motion.</li>
  <li>Headings follow a single logical order per page, and page regions use landmarks.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="limits">3. Known limitations</h2>
<p>Stated plainly rather than glossed over:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The GitHub activity graph</strong> on the <a href="/code/">Code</a> page is rendered by a third-party
    widget whose markup I do not control. Its tooltips and colour scale may not meet AA. The same information is
    available directly on
    <a href="https://github.com/steftzor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my GitHub profile</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>The GitHub statistics cards</strong> are images generated by an external service. Their alternative text
    describes what they show, but the individual numbers inside them are not exposed as text.</li>
  <li><strong>The animated hero background</strong> on the home page is decorative and hidden from screen readers. It is
    disabled when reduced motion is requested.</li>
  <li>Testing has been done manually and with automated tooling, not with a formal third-party audit or a full range of
    assistive technologies.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="feedback">4. Tell me if something blocks you</h2>
<p>
  If any part of this site is difficult or impossible for you to use, email
  <a href="mailto:stefanos@tzortzoglou.eu">stefanos@tzortzoglou.eu</a> and say which page and what happened. I will fix
  what I can and tell you honestly if something is outside my control.
</p>
